  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which bleomycin may interact with T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3, through a series of molecular interactions involving palmarumycin CP18. Bleomycin is known to have a target of HT-144, MCF-10A, and COLO-792, all of which are implicated in the target of palmarumycin CP18. This compound, in turn, is linked to the T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3, indicating a possible pathway where bleomycin may exert its effects via palmarumycin CP18. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent relationship, though the strength of the evidence is moderate, with some variation in the scores across the different paths. The mechanism appears to involve a chain of targets, where bleomycin's interaction is mediated through palmarumycin CP18, which then affects CD3. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, but further validation would be needed to confirm the direct interaction between bleomycin and CD3.",
